The Association of American Universities calls out yet another
self-defeating proposal from this Congress. Supporters of things like this,
please help me understand. Is the goal to start with something horrendous,
hope the other side agrees to meet you in the middle, and then end up with
something moderately counterproductive =E2=80=94 as opposed to horrendously
counterproductive =E2=80=94 to national interests?

*The SAFE Research Act would have far-ranging impacts affecting all
research agencies, not just the Department of Defense. It would create such
enormously broad definitions of =E2=80=9Chostile foreign entity=E2=80=9D an=
d =E2=80=9Caffiliation=E2=80=9D
that would apply to any agreement that a U.S. university has with any
university in China or other defined countries at the time of application
or in the five years prior to application. This would include collaborative
work with any individual faculty member or former student who subsequently
returned to China as a required condition of their U.S. visa. It would
capture every single research agreement, every study abroad program, every
language program, every professional conference, and every campus facility
that a U.S. university might have in partnership with another institution
abroad.*

