ols, just One Year after its Birth</a></strong></h2><p style=3D"margin:0 0 =
20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>Context=
: </strong><span>In November 2024, Anthropic released a technology update t=
hat largely escaped the headlines. Anthropic=E2=80=99s Model Context Protoc=
ol (MCP) acts like a USB port for AI applications. Just like your computer=
=E2=80=99s USB port allows it to exchange data with other devices (e.g., a =
phone) as well as connect to add-ons (e.g., a mouse, an external monitor), =
MCP provides a </span><em>standardized</em><span> set of procedures that en=
able one company=E2=80=99s AI agents to connect to data sources and tools f=
rom other companies.</span></p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,5=
5,55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><span>The MCP standard could develop=
 into a globally interoperable interface that allows AI model builders to c=
onnect with developers of complementary products, thereby growing the overa=
ll AI ecosystem. The potential economies of scale have attracted even Anthr=
opic=E2=80=99s fiercest rivals to adopt the protocol. In fact, Chinese AI g=
iants Baidu, Alibaba, and Tencent all embraced MCP before Google and OpenAI=
 </span><strong><a href=3D"https://substack.com/redirect/f9158678-b939-4782=
-9590-7860ab0735d8?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJ=
m_FAk3tf6E" rel=3D"" style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);text-decoration:underline=
" target=3D"_blank">followed suit</a></strong><span>. There are numerous tu=
torials that guide users through employing MCP to link their main AI app wi=
th China=E2=80=99s DeepSeek R1 model and take advantage of its advanced rea=
soning capabilities.</span></p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,5=
5,55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><span>In this week=E2=80=99s transla=
tion of a Gui Xingren [=E7=A1=85=E6=98=9F=E4=BA=BA] article (link to </span=
><strong><a href=3D"https://substack.com/redirect/699ff0e7-4552-4609-a5bd-5=
09e5ba85c0f?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3t=
f6E" rel=3D"" style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);text-decoration:underline" targe=
t=3D"_blank">original Chinese</a></strong><span>), Dongdao Li provides an o=
ne-year-in update on MCP. Previously, I=E2=80=99ve translated a Gui Xingren=
 analysis of Chinese procurement data to evaluate the diffusion of large mo=
dels to government-facing applications (</span><strong><a href=3D"https://s=
ubstack.com/redirect/a2fd43aa-fe3a-4b1d-8446-c59aa922ec95?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZse=
DYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E" rel=3D"" style=3D"color:=
rgb(54,55,55);text-decoration:underline" target=3D"_blank">ChinAI #275</a><=
/strong><span>). </span></p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,5=
5);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>Key Takeaways: The promise of M=
CP channels why technical standards are essential infrastructure for modula=
r technology ecosystems. </strong></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0">=
<li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-heig=
ht:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16=
px;margin:0"><span>Li explains: =E2=80=9C</span><em>Before MCP, if develope=
rs wanted Claude to access Google Drive, they had to write a set of code to=
 connect to the API. If they wanted it to access Slack? They had to write a=
nother API. It was even worse for IDE (integrated development environment) =
vendors; Cursor (popular AI code editor) had to be adapted to Linear (a pro=
ject management tool), Windsurf (another AI coding assistant) had to be ada=
pted to Linear, and everyone was doing almost the exact same dirty work</em=
><span>.=E2=80=9D</span></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=
=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-=
box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0">In the MCP Era, Linear can ju=
st build one MCP server,, and any AI agent, developed by any company, can p=
lug in.</p></li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line=
-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>However, when promise meets real-world=
 engineering implementation, MPC has cooled off.</strong></p><ul style=3D"m=
argin-top:0;padding:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:=
rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;paddin=
g-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0">Li writes, =E2=80=9CEveryone knows how =
expensive Claude=E2=80=99s tokens are; loading too many MCPs before even ge=
nerating any content results in significant costs.=E2=80=9D The article cit=
es a Simon Willison blog post (linked in Four to Forward section), which po=
ints out that GitHub=E2=80=99s official MCP includes 93 different tools tha=
t cost 55,000 tokens. </p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=
=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-=
box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0">When AI agents have to call t=
oo many MCPs, they can malfunction and hallucinate. In some cases, they hav=
e accidentally deleted codebases. Li also references a research preprint th=
at analyzed around 1,900 MCP servers, finding numerous issues such as lack =
of maintenance and exposed credentials.</p></li></ul><div style=3D"font-siz=
e:16px;line-height:26px;margin:32px auto"><table width=3D"100%" border=3D"0=
